# Phase 6 -- slot rollback on backtrack (CHOICE, committed branch). The first
# choice alternative captures a word via (defer s W) and the required "X"
# matches, so the alternative COMMITS. The deferred item must survive, so the
# (parse-deferred s Body) drain invokes Body exactly once. The companion of
# slot-rollback-choice-fail: rollback discards on failure but keeps on success.
<<<cmd
printf 'hello X\nbody\n' | "$TP" run test/suite/lexgoal/slot-rollback-choice.scm --input - --dump-tree
<<<assert
exit 0
out-count 1 Body [
out-count 0 Extra [
out-contains line: W
out-absent ERROR
